  "summary": {
    "as": "Introduced in House",
    "asOf": "2026-07-09",
    "date": "2026-09-10T20:43:14Z",
    "text": "Coordinating and Harnessing America\u2019s Recovery of Minerals Act or the CHARM Act\n\nThis bill requires the Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) to establish and carry out a national strategy for recovering critical minerals\u00a0from discarded materials. Critical minerals are defined as any mineral, element, substance, or material designated as critical by the U.S. Geological Survey because it is essential to U.S. economic or national security, has a vulnerable supply chain, and serves an essential function in manufacturing a product.\n\nThe EPA must report to Congress every two years on its actions, plans, and recommendations relating to the national strategy."
  },
